https://opencv.org  —  https://github.com/opencv/opencv
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
(OpenCV was BSD-3-Clause before release 4.5.0; confirm which applies to the
version this project's implementation was derived from.)

    The bilinear resampler in internal/plate/preprocess.go reproduces OpenCV's
    generic C++ INTER_LINEAR path for 8-bit input: fixed-point interpolation
    weights at a 1<<11 scale (INTER_RESIZE_COEF_BITS), the two-truncation
    vertical accumulate, and the asymmetric edge handling between the two axes
    — the horizontal coefficient loop clamps the interpolation fraction to
    zero, while the vertical axis preserves the fraction and clamps only the
    row index. resizePlanar, linearCoefficients and verticalLinear implement
    that behaviour.

